From: VyOS LS1046A maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 0147] dpaa: handle TC_SETUP_FT in ndo_setup_tc for nft flowtable offload

Root cause: nft 'flags offload' -> nf_flow_table_offload_setup() sees that
the DPAA1 netdev has ndo_setup_tc (from board patch 0104) and takes the
nf_flow_table_offload_cmd() path, which calls ndo_setup_tc(dev, TC_SETUP_FT).
But dpaa_setup_tc() only handles TC_SETUP_QDISC_MQPRIO and TC_SETUP_BLOCK;
TC_SETUP_FT falls through to default -> -EOPNOTSUPP.

Fix: route TC_SETUP_FT to the existing dpaa_setup_tc_block() handler, which
already understands flow_block_cb_alloc/add/remove via the upstream flow_block
infrastructure. The two tc_setup_type enums are semantically identical for
flowtable block binds (nft flowtables use CLSACT_INGRESS binder on kernel 6.18,
which dpaa_setup_tc_block() already accepts).

Required for: CONFIG_NF_FLOW_TABLE_OFFLOAD=m (board commit 8d37d54) to
unblock the kernel->ask.ko REPLACE handler trigger chain.

Signed-off-by: VyOS LS1046A maintainers
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
@@ dpaa_setup_tc: add TC_SETUP_FT case @@
 static int dpaa_setup_tc(struct net_device *net_dev, enum tc_setup_type type,
 			 void *type_data)
 {
 	switch (type) {
 	case TC_SETUP_QDISC_MQPRIO:
 		return dpaa_setup_tc_mqprio(net_dev, type_data);
 	case TC_SETUP_BLOCK:
 		return dpaa_setup_tc_block(net_dev, type_data);
+	case TC_SETUP_FT:
+		return dpaa_setup_tc_block(net_dev, type_data);
 	default:
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	}
 }
